{{- /*
  The `twin` format's producer, wired only by the `unpublished` environment.

  It renders NOTHING for a page carrying `twin: false`, which is how a wired
  format and a published document come apart: Hugo writes no file for a
  zero-byte render, reports that nowhere, and keeps reporting the format on the
  page with a resolving .RelPermalink. Its answer to the manifest lives beside
  it in _partials/url-retirement/publishes/twin.html.
*/ -}}
{{- /*
  It also registers a URL from a format's OWN pass, which is the one way a
  registration is lost. `twin` carries no weight, so it renders after the
  weight-100 manifest, and the URL below is refused with a warning instead of
  being accepted into a map nothing reads again. The path names no file in the
  tree on purpose: if the refusal ever stopped working, the manifest would carry
  a URL this build never wrote, and the assertion comparing the manifest against
  the published tree would say so.

  The call is outside the branch below and fully trimmed, so it changes the
  rendered byte length of neither arm -- and a zero-byte render is exactly what
  the `twin: false` page is here to produce.
*/ -}}
{{- partial "url-retirement/register-url.html" (dict "page" . "url" "/probe/registered-too-late.txt") -}}
{{- if ne .Params.twin false -}}
TWIN {{ .Title }}
{{ end -}}
